 "title": "Saccharomyces cerevisiae Response to Heat Stress",
 "summary": "This cluster focuses on Saccharomyces cerevisiae's response to heat stress, specifically heat ramp and heat shock. The organism exhibits both processes and has heat shock factor Hsf1. Hsf1 de-represses Sis1 and represses Hsp70, which acts with Sis1. The transcriptome is affected by both heat ramp and heat shock, and DEGs are detected in these processes. DEGs correspond to ESR, and Hsf1 is enriched in WGCNA, which uses ComBat. YGP1 is carried by a plasmid, co-regulated with HSP26, and induced by Msn2 and Msn4. Puf5 regulates Haa1 and is dependent on Ixr1. The organism's response to heat stress is studied by Megumi Sato.",
